  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Expanding Cold Storage Facility - Senegal</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This Dutch SME intends to invest in the expansion of an existing cold storage facility for potatoes, onions, carrots and other products in Senegal. Together with an investment in a new packing service provider.For these investments DGGF is planning to provide a loan to the Dutch company. Through the intended investments the company wants to answer to the increasing demand for cold storage by local farmers. On top of that this storage will secure the quality and extend the durability of these products. Besides this impact, the project will create approximately 15 jobs, of which 8 for women, and approximately 20 seasonal jobs. Employees will be fully trained to manage and maintain the facility, to operate forklifts and other equipment. Full instruction on (food)safety and hygiene will also be given to all personnel.This project will contribute to theSustainable Development Goals: 1 &#x2013; 2 - 8 and 12.</narrative>
  </description>
